-+++ /mnt/data/chtReactingNanoParcelFoam/README.md	2026-09-03 09:59:27.601541452 +0000
-@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
-+# chtReactingNanoParcelFoam (OpenFOAM-v2406)
-+
-+This solver merges the uploaded `chtMultiRegionFoam` with the uploaded
-+`reactingNanoParcelFoam` Lagrangian implementation.
-+
-+## What is coupled
-+
-+For every fluid region, the solver constructs:
-+
-+- `rhoReactionThermo`
-+- `SLGThermo`
-+- one `basicReactingTypeCloud` named `reactingCloud1`
-+- one Eulerian `surfaceFilmModel`
-+
-+The parcel cloud is advanced **once per physical time step**, before the
-+PIMPLE/CHT outer iterations. Its source terms are then reused while the
-+Eulerian equations and fluid-solid heat transfer converge at that time level.
-+
-+Parcel/film source terms included in the carrier equations:
-+
-+- continuity: `parcels.Srho(rho)` and `surfaceFilm.Srho()`
-+- pressure/continuity correction: `parcels.Srho()` and `surfaceFilm.Srho()`
-+- momentum: `parcels.SU(U)`
-+- species: `parcels.SYi(i,Yi)` and `surfaceFilm.Srho(i)`
-+- energy: `parcels.Sh(he)` and `surfaceFilm.Sh()`
-+
-+The original CHT energy matrix assembly is retained, so parcel enthalpy source
-+terms participate directly in conjugate fluid-solid energy coupling.
-+
-+## Preserved split-solve controls
-+
-+Under `PIMPLE` in each fluid region's `fvSolution`:
-+
-+```text
-+solveFlow      true;   // optional; if present, overrides frozenFlow
-+solveSpecies   true;   // default true
-+solveEnergy    true;   // default true
-+```
-+
-+`solveFlow false` maps to frozen-flow operation, but unlike stock
-+`chtMultiRegionFoam`, species can still be advanced. This preserves the useful
-+behaviour of the uploaded `reactingNanoParcelFoam` for fixed-flow scalar and
-+thermal calculations.
-+
-+For energy-coupled CHT, `solveEnergy` must be `true`.
-+
-+## Surface film when you do not use a film
-+
-+The Eulerian surface-film framework is retained because the uploaded nano
-+solver couples its mass/species/energy source terms. OpenFOAM's `none` model
-+can be used when no film is required.
-+
-+For each fluid region, create `constant/<fluidRegion>/surfaceFilmProperties`
-+with at least:
-+
-+```text
-+FoamFile
-+{
-+    format      ascii;
-+    class       dictionary;
-+    object      surfaceFilmProperties;
-+}
-+
-+surfaceFilmModel none;
-+```
-+
-+The Lagrangian cloud's own `surfaceFilmModel` in
-+`reactingCloud1Properties` can likewise remain `none` when not used.
-+
-+## Cloud properties location
-+
-+Because this is a multi-region solver, each fluid region is its own object
-+registry. The `reactingCloud1` dictionary and any fields used by custom parcel
-+forces should therefore belong to that fluid region, e.g.
-+
-+```text
-+constant/<fluidRegion>/reactingCloud1Properties
-+```
-+
-+and fields such as an electric field used by `CoulombForce` should be placed
-+in the corresponding region time directory.
-+
-+## Closed-volume mass handling
-+
-+Stock `chtMultiRegionFoam` fixes the absolute pressure level of a closed fluid
-+region using the initial carrier-gas mass. That is inconsistent when parcels
-+or a film transfer mass to/from the gas.
-+
-+This merged solver therefore maintains `targetMassFluid`. Once per physical
-+time step it updates the target carrier mass with the volume-integrated
-+`parcels.Srho()` and `surfaceFilm.Srho()` sources. The closed-volume pressure
-+correction uses this updated target mass.
-+
-+## Build
-+
-+Load the OpenFOAM-v2406 environment first, then from this directory:
-+
-+```bash
-+./Allwmake
-+```
-+
-+The script builds the bundled modified Lagrangian libraries first and then:
-+
-+```text
-+$FOAM_USER_APPBIN/chtReactingNanoParcelFoam
-+```
-+
-+To clean:
-+
-+```bash
-+./Allwclean
-+```
-+
-+## Recommended first validation
-+
-+Do not start with the final T-junction case. Validate in this order:
-+
-+1. **CHT only / no parcels**
-+   - no parcel injection
-+   - `surfaceFilmModel none`
-+   - compare `U`, `p`, `T` and solid `T` against stock `chtMultiRegionFoam`.
-+
-+2. **One-way parcels**
-+   - set the cloud solution to uncoupled
-+   - verify trajectories against `reactingNanoParcelFoam` using the same
-+     carrier fields.
-+
-+3. **Two-way parcel sources**
-+   - enable cloud coupling
-+   - check integrated carrier + parcel mass and energy balances.
-+
-+4. **Final T-junction CHT + supersaturation problem**
-+   - activate wall heating/cooling and the required vapour species.
-+
-+## Important scope
-+
-+This version uses the static multi-region mesh architecture of the supplied
-+`chtMultiRegionFoam`. The uploaded `reactingNanoParcelFoam` dynamic-mesh
-+operations are **not** transplanted into the multi-region solver. For the
-+static T-shaped mixer discussed in this project this is intentional.
-+
-+All custom Lagrangian source directories needed by the uploaded nano solver
-+are bundled (`distributionModels`, `basic`, `intermediate`, `turbulence`).
-+Generated `lnInclude` links and old object files are intentionally omitted;
-+`wmake` regenerates them on Linux.
