+
+## 2026-09-07: steady-state / solveParcels controls
+
+This reviewed version supports two deliberately separated operating modes.
+
+### A. Steady carrier + species + CHT (recommended for obtaining a converged field)
+
+Use `steadyState` as the **default ddt scheme in every fluid and solid region** and set, in each fluid-region `fvSolution`:
+
+```text
+PIMPLE
+{
+    nOuterCorrectors          3;
+    nCorrectors               1;
+    nNonOrthogonalCorrectors  0;
+
+    solveFlow       true;
+    solveSpecies    true;
+    solveEnergy     true;
+    solveParcels    false;
+}
+```
+
+In this mode:
+
+- `SLGThermo` and `reactingCloud1` are not constructed;
+- no parcel dictionary/submodel is read;
+- no `parcels.evolve()` occurs;
+- parcel `SU`, `SYi`, `Sh`, `Srho` sources are absent;
+- the transient `rhoEqn` is not solved;
+- a steady pressure correction adapted from the v2406
+  `chtMultiRegionSimpleFoam` pressure equation is used;
+- Courant/Diffusion based physical-time step adjustment is skipped.
+
+For a convenient iteration counter use, for example, `deltaT 1` and
+`adjustTimeStep no` in `controlDict`. In steady mode the Time value is an
+iteration/pseudo-time label, not physical residence time.
+
+### B. Transient carrier + reacting nano parcels
+
+Use a transient ddt scheme (`Euler`, `backward`, etc.) in all regions and set
+`solveParcels true`. The original two-way parcel source coupling is retained.
+
+`solveParcels` is a startup-only switch. Restart the solver to change it.
+This avoids constructing/destructing the cloud dynamically in the middle of a
+run.
+
+### C. Recommended two-stage workflow
+
+1. Run Mode A to convergence.
+2. Copy/restart from the converged carrier/solid fields.
+3. Change all regions to a transient ddt scheme, set `solveParcels true`, and
+   if desired set `solveFlow/solveSpecies/solveEnergy` according to the desired
+   one-way/two-way coupling strategy.
+
+### Pure-water Fuchs-Knudsen phase change
+
+The supplied `LiquidEvapFuchsKnudsen.C` also contains the previously required
+pure-liquid correction. `solution (H2O);` is valid and no longer dereferences a
+non-existent second (solid) component. A two-component `(liquid solid)`
+solution remains supported.
